<%# The bar an original in the archive wears: the way back, and the one
    decision this page can record. Held mail wears the pen's bar instead,
    whose two endings are what a hold has and where muting would be the wrong
    answer — a sender the reader never subscribed to is dismissed, not muted.

    Back pointed at the reader until the reader was deleted. Where it goes now
    depends on where the mail lives rather than on where the reader came from:
    the archive for content, the pen for a dismissed confirmation, which
    Newsletter.content keeps off the archive while the new-senders list still
    links to it. The presenter owns that choice and the label with it.

    Muting is a POST, so it is a button_to and has to stop looking like one —
    the same shape the pen bar's two actions wear. It mutes the sender rather
    than this issue: the decision is about who writes, and the issue stays
    exactly where it is. %>
<header class="topbar">
  <%= link_to newsletter.back_label,
        newsletter.back_path,
        class: "topbar__back" %>

  <div class="topbar__actions">
    <%= button_to t("newsletters.original.silence"),
          newsletter_silence_path(newsletter),
          class: "topbar__action",
          form_class: "topbar__form" %>
  </div>
</header>
